  486: 
  487: # Decoupling D4k (social review M-1): a manager's member functions are defined in manager files.
  488: # The rules above are per FILE, so a member declared in a manager header but defined in an owner
  489: # file could read the character under the manager's name and no gate would see it (and in
  490: # mangos_tests, which cannot find a character, it would quietly do nothing). So every class or
  491: # struct DEFINED in a MANAGER_FILES header is a manager class, and a definition of one of its
  492: # members -- a line that starts in column 0, spells `Class::member(` and does not end in ';' -- in
  493: # any other file under src/game fails, unless OWNER_DEFINED names that member in that file. An
  494: # unchangeable caller is the only reason for an entry (README, "Manager shape" 6). The list is a
  495: # ratchet: an entry whose file no longer defines the member fails, and so does a second definition
  496: # of a listed member in its file (an overload would otherwise ride on the entry).
  497: # Entries: "<Class>::<member>|<file relative to src/game>".
